// Capability- and Provenance-Driven Alias Analysis (`AliasInfo`) Engine (T606 / E15.2).
// Implements SPEC-71 §1 (AXS-ALIAS-001..005, AXS-ESC-017) & SPEC-70 (AXS-OPT-021..022):
//   - 5-value `AliasResult` lattice (`NoAlias`, `MustAlias`, `PartialAlias`, `MayAlias`, `UnknownAlias`)
//   - 6-value spatial `RegionRelation` (`Disjoint`, `Same`, `Contains`, `ContainedBy`, `Overlaps`, `Unknown`)
//   - Verified `mut_view<T>` disjointness (`ALIAS_REASON_CAP_MUT_DISJOINT`, `REQ-OPT-299`, `REQ-OPT-358`)
//   - `view<T>` read-only stability intervals (`ALIAS_REASON_CAP_VIEW_READONLY`, `REQ-OPT-301`)
//   - 3-tier structural disjointness: allocation roots, field trees, constant/RangeInfo slice intervals (`REQ-OPT-303`)
//   - Strict fail-closed handling of raw pointers, shared owners, dynamic indices, and FFI (`REQ-OPT-028`, `REQ-OPT-300`, `REQ-OPT-314`)
//   - Zero-copy / DMA / mmap active capability lifetime & non-aliasing verification (`REQ-OPT-347`)
